course: dictionary
lesson: 12870
title: Enraged and strong feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Enraged» is a strong word for anger. It means extremely angry, full of rage. Cross and annoyed are small feelings. Enraged is a big one.
explain: «The enraged bull charged at the red gate.» The word tells you the bull is not just grumpy. It is dangerous. Try swapping in «cross» and see how much the sentence loses its power.
explain: Enrage is also a verb, and enraged is its past form. «The lie enraged Sam» means the lie made Sam extremely angry. Look for who or what caused the anger, because the verb needs a cause.
fact: Enraged means extremely angry, full of rage.
fact: Enraged is also the past form of the verb enrage, which means to make someone extremely angry.
fact: Enraged is much stronger than cross or annoyed.
fact: «Enraged by» and «enraged at» tell you what caused the anger, as in «enraged by the news».
fact: In nature writing, an enraged animal, such as a bull or a bear, can be dangerous.
exercise: «The enraged bull charged at the red gate.» What does enraged mean? | *Extremely angry | Lost and scared | Hungry for grass | Very tired
exercise: «The crowd was enraged by the unfair decision.» What made the crowd angry? | The long wait | The sunny weather | The new shoes | *The unfair decision
exercise: «Mia's little brother broke her model, and it enraged her.» Here enraged is a verb form. What does it mean? | Made her hungry | Made her feel calm and relaxed | Made her bored of the game | *Made her extremely angry
test: «Dad was enraged at the broken window.» Which word is closest in meaning to enraged? | *Furious | Sleepy | Pleased
test: Which sentence uses enraged correctly? | The enraged cake was delicious. | I enraged a sandwich at lunch. | *The enraged dog barked and pulled at its lead.
exam: Which word is the best swap for enraged in «She was enraged when she lost the race»? | Mildly annoyed | Bored | Happy | *Furious
